meta {
  name: negative
}

docs {
  Adversarial and error-path requests: wrong client authentication method, malformed/garbage tokens, a resource read with an unrequested scope, expired or misdirected client assertions, invalid `authorization_details` (unknown type, two contexts, malformed JSON, missing identifier, trailing content, unknown field — all 400 `invalid_authorization_details`), an unsupported grant type, an onboarded hospital whose `jwks_url` is unreachable locally, and the Resource Server context rules (resource outside the context graph, a context the caller is not party to, a foreign `Task.requester`). Each documents an expected rejection — except `15-get-token-foreign-context`, the setup for 16, which shows that the AS issues a token for any context because counter-party entitlement is a Resource Server obligation.

  See each request's own docs block for the exact behavior and its RFC/IG backing. Some requests here reuse tokens obtained in `auth/`.
}
